Z||000011||dennis_6||10-15-2001||05:27 AM||||Do not use a 3.4 FWD engine as it will be DOHC and you will not be able to use your old engine parts.  Which means custom wiring, cutting your right decklid support, a new computer, and the entire engine not just the block.  The 3.1 FWD will work though... found in old minivans!!!||||reg||1
Z||000012||Raydar||10-15-2001||08:50 AM||||Don't use a 3400 block either. The pistons are different. If you bolt on the Fiero heads, you'll have 7.x:1 compression. And you can't bolt the Fiero intake to the 3400's aluminum heads, either.   <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
